LC 88 - Merge Sorted Array
Pattern: Two Pointers
// Time: O(m + n)
// Space: O(1)

ALGO:
Start from the end of both arrays.
Compare nums1[m-1] and nums2[n-1].
Put the larger element at the end of nums1.
Move that pointer backward.
Continue until nums2 is completely merged.

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    void merge(vector<int>& nums1, int m, vector<int>& nums2, int n) {
        int i = m - 1, j = n - 1, k = m + n - 1;

        while (j >= 0) {
            if (i >= 0 && nums1[i] > nums2[j])
                nums1[k--] = nums1[i--];
            else
                nums1[k--] = nums2[j--];
        }
    }
};

EX:
[1,2,3,0,0,0]
[2,5,6]

6 → end
5 → end
3 → end
2 → end
2 → end
1 → end

[1,2,2,3,5,6] ✅






